# raw requests: https://drive.google.com/file/d/102AFIHkEQHuvG8-hZeWHVFqXeeI-a8xS (R5.zip), sha256 5825f74443cf6e4f5df264f8c94d439fc9eae576399f9786a50ca4cb3316e60d
# sandboxes: Huawei's serverless pods (possibly containers), taken as microVM requests by shape: launch, lifetime, CPU, memory, owner
# 25295 pods launched by cold starts on day 30; 25295 sandboxes traced; 339 owners (userID), each of weight 1; 468 functions
# lifetime: cold start to the end of the pod's last request of the day, plus 60 s keep-alive (Huawei's pods keep alive 60 s after each request, Joosen et al. §2)
# cold starts whose pod ID names no pool, left out: 48
# second cold starts of a pod already launched, left out: 2
# shapes (millicores, MB): 300/128: 16937, 400/256: 2868, 1800/2048: 1184, 600/512: 1157, 3400/4096: 894, 6600/8192: 480, 800/768: 477, 2600/3072: 428, 3000/3584: 150, 1000/1024: 144, 1200/1280: 144, 1400/1536: 144, 1600/1792: 144, 2200/2560: 144
# classes by owner, a third of the launches each: oci 8432, firecracker 8432, shards 8431
# overheads: oci 0.42 MiB (Hex, bench/competitive/RESULT.md:95), firecracker 5 MiB (its specification and Agache et al. NSDI 2020, substrates-and-sandboxes.md §3.3), shards by guest size, 128 MiB: 2.26, 256 MiB: 2.29, 512 MiB: 2.31, 768 MiB: 2.33, 1024 MiB: 2.34, 1280 MiB: 2.61, 1536 MiB: 2.64, 1792 MiB: 2.61, 2048 MiB: 2.68, 2560 MiB: 3.02, 3072 MiB: 2.99, 3584 MiB: 3.37, 4096 MiB: 3.63, 8192 MiB: 4.77 MiB (measured on fedora under KVM: Shards a0cced87, its VMM's own PSS beside 5 idle guests plus the kernel's memory per guest; bench/sched/shards_overhead.md)
# nodes: 10 x EC2 m5d.metal (48 cores, 384 GiB, no GPU; Agache et al., NSDI 2020 §6), Linux x86_64 with KVM, each running all three classes
